lesson:
A FUNCTION is a named, reusable spell:
    int heal(int hp, int amount) { return hp + amount; }
  return type  name  (parameters)  { body }
  'void' means it returns nothing.
  Parameters are COPIES by default. Use & (reference) to modify the original:
    void boost(int& mana) { mana += 10; }

lessonCode:
int square(int n) {
    return n * n;
}

void greet(std::string name) {
    std::cout << "Hail, " << name;
}

int main() {
    int s = square(4);   // 16
    greet("Morgana");
}

